"""Layer-0 MLP down-projection component 3340: a "walking" detector.

The component writes a large negative value into the residual stream on tokens that
mean walking (on foot), and a weaker negative on related verbs. Everywhere else it is
near zero, apart from small diffuse noise that this program does not model.

- 走 (walk / go on foot) is the strongest trigger: about -6.6 alone, about -5.5 in 走了,
  and about -2 to -3 in compounds such as 走到, 走向, 走出.
- English walk words (walk, walks, walked, walking, Walking) give about -1.5.
- 跑 (run) gives about -1.2 and 穿 (wear, or pass through) about -0.8.
- Motion-away words (away, gone, moving) give a faint -0.3.

